  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Protection of Civilians and Respect for the Rule of Law in Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This funding supports the work of the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) in PNG, according to the annual Pacific Appeals. ICRC work promotes respect for International Humanitarian Law (IHL) and other international norms among armed and security forces. It works to ensure violence affected communities and individuals can access emergency aid and medical care.  The focus of the activities is the Highlands provinces such as Enga, with some activities supporting the setup of Office of Missing Persons in Bougainville.</narrative>
  </description>
